source: crates/yojaka-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8(out.stdout).unwrap()"
---
Index, de-duplicate and organize photos & videos

Usage: yojaka [OPTIONS] [PATH] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  scan      Scan a folder; only new and changed files are read
  stats     Show statistics for a scanned folder
  info      Show metadata for one file, including GPS and place
  places    List the places (countries and cities) found in the library
  export    Export the file list as CSV or JSON (GPS is left out unless --include-gps)
  dupes     Find duplicates (Iteration 4)
  organize  Organize into a folder template (Iteration 6)
  plan      Inspect plans (Iteration 5)
  apply     Execute a plan (Iteration 5)
  undo      Undo an applied plan (Iteration 5)
  history   List executed plans (Iteration 5)
  doctor    Check the environment and print paths
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [PATH]  Folder or volume to open (default: current dir)

Options:
      --write              Allow write operations (still requires dry-run + confirm)
      --refresh            Scan on open if the last scan is over an hour old (never clears anything)
      --force              Ask first, then forget what is saved about the folder and scan it from
                           scratch (slower)
      --threads <THREADS>  Worker threads (default: auto)
  -h, --help               Print help
  -V, --version            Print version
